  1168	      "contemporaneous|D_down",
  1169	      "contemporaneous|F"
  1170	    ],
  1171	    "the_null_comparison_is_INCONCLUSIVE": "The variants split. Worse, the pre-registered primary's own non-rejection is not strong evidence: the mechanism diagnostic shows variant A's null manufactures its 0.619 decline by letting plain decay cross the fixed 2-point threshold at high vol levels (null within-regime shock rate 0.82 at crisis vs the data's 0.54), which is NOT how the decline arises in the data. A's 'pass' is one artifact cancelling another. The corrected nulls (B frequency-matched, C relative-threshold, G doubly-corrected) all reject. So neither 'the decline is pure GARCH mechanics' NOR 'the decline is absorption' is established by the null comparison. It is inconclusive, and saying otherwise in either direction would be overclaiming.",
  1172	    "why_no_null_can_settle_the_down_side": "Below 28.8 annualised points this null cannot produce a vol-DOWN shock AT ALL (alpha=0 => the deepest one-day fall is pure decay). But the empirical decline is carried ENTIRELY by vol-DOWN days. On the down side the null and the data are not even measuring the same event, so where B/C/G reject, what they detect is the ABSENCE OF A RELIEF-RALLY CHANNEL IN GARCH -- not the PRESENCE OF ABSORPTION IN MARKETS."
  1173	  },
  1174	  "null_free_evidence": {
  1175	    "pooled_decline_headline": 0.8165,
  1176	    "up_only_decline": -0.1226,
  1177	    "up_only_decline_ci95": [
  1178	      -0.7289,
  1179	      0.5828
  1180	    ],
  1181	    "up_only_ci_excludes_pooled_headline": true,
  1182	    "down_only_decline": 1.3368,
  1183	    "n_calm_up_shocks": 10,
  1184	    "n_calm_down_shocks": 24,
  1185	    "finding": "Split the shock set by the SIGN of the VIX move and the paper's mechanism evaporates. Pooled decline 0.8165. Among genuine FEAR SPIKES (dVIX>+2) the decline is -0.1226, bootstrap 95% CI [-0.7289, 0.5828] -- it contains ZERO (no absorption gradient can be established) AND its upper end sits BELOW the pooled headline 0.8165, so the headline is significantly larger than anything fear spikes can account for. The decline lives in the RELIEF RALLIES (dVIX<-2): 1.3368. And the calm anchor that sets the headline's magnitude rests on 10 fear-spike days against 24 relief days. This holds with NO null model, so it is immune to every calibration dispute above.",
  1186	    "mechanism": "A 2-point VIX fall from 13 is a rare, large relief move that comes with a big rally; a 2-point fall from 27 is routine mean reversion with an ordinary return. So the shock bucket's mean |r| is inflated at calm levels and deflated at high levels -- SAR declines. That is signed-composition selection, not fear being absorbed."
  1187	  },
  1188	  "pre_registered_primary_outcome": "IDENTIFICATION CLOSED",
  1189	  "pre_registered_primary_detail": "Empirical decline 0.8165 falls INSIDE the contemporaneous null 95% CI [0.0824, 1.0596] (MC p=0.409759). A GJR-GARCH with no absorption mechanism, once its vol proxy is made contemporaneous with returns the way VIX is, reproduces the observed SAR decline. Per the pre-registered rule the absorption claim is DOWNGRADED to a mechanical decomposition of fixed-threshold selection plus same-day co-movement; K897's NULL REJECTED verdict does not survive the timing fix.",
  1190	  "verdict": "ABSORPTION CLAIM NOT SUPPORTED",
  1191	  "verdict_detail": "Three findings, in order of how much weight they can bear.\n\n(1) NULL-FREE, DECISIVE -- the paper's mechanism is not what drives its statistic. Splitting shocks by the sign of the VIX move: the pooled decline is 0.8165, but among genuine FEAR SPIKES it is -0.1226 with bootstrap 95% CI [-0.7289, 0.5828] -- containing zero AND lying entirely below the pooled headline. The decline lives in the RELIEF RALLIES (1.3368). The calm anchor rests on 10 fear-spike days vs 24 relief days. 'Ambient fear absorbs fear shocks' is therefore not what the SAR decline shows, and this conclusion depends on NO null model.\n\n(2) THE NULL COMPARISON IS INCONCLUSIVE, in both directions. The pre-registered primary (variant A) does not reject (0.8165 inside [0.0824, 1.0596], p=0.409759), so by the letter of the pre-registered rule the absorption claim is downgraded. But A's null earns its decline by letting plain decay cross the fixed 2-point threshold at high vol -- an artifact, not the data's mechanism -- so its non-rejection is two artifacts cancelling. The corrected nulls (B, C, G) all reject. Neither 'it is just GARCH' nor 'it is absorption' is established by the null comparison.\n\n(3) K897'S VERDICT DOES NOT SURVIVE REGARDLESS. Its NULL REJECTED rested on a null whose vol proxy could not react to the same day's return; on the same seeds and params, making the proxy contemporaneous moves the null's SAR levels from ~1.0-1.2 to ~1.6-2.4 and its decline from 0.1734 to 0.619. The margin K897 reported was largely a timing artifact.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: the paper cannot claim absorption. It CAN claim something real and publishable -- that the SAR regime-decline is a signed-composition effect, and that it is NOT reproduced by a well-specified GARCH null (B/C/G reject). That is a measurement note, not the absorption hypothesis."
  1192	}
